[[Gerrit Rietveld]], Netherlands. Designed in 1917, painted in its colors in the early 1920s.

Painted wood. Two flat boards for the seat and back, held in a frame of straight sticks. Red, blue, yellow, black.

No carving, no upholstery, and no reference to any chair that came before. The idea was a form anyone anywhere would read the same way.

What is it arguing?
